  "id": "tastant",
  "term": "tastant",
  "definition": "A tastant is a substance used as a taste stimulus, such as monosodium glutamate, to produce and study a particular taste experience. In this context, it refers to a component that is ingested so researchers can examine taste perception and related brain responses.",
